  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Universidad Antonio De Nebrija (Nebrija University) is a private institution in Madrid, Spain, that combines academic tradition with innovation. You’ll find that the university has been named after the humanist Antonio de Nebrija. Here, you can select your course from a wide range of programs in business, communication, engineering, and international relations.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>As a student at Nebrija University, you become part of a close-knit, international community. You’ll find plenty of chances to meet people from all over the world. The university offers you a variety of student clubs and extracurricular activities, including the Debate Club, the Entrepreneurs Club, the Art Club, and many more.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>The university offers you modern student residences with essential amenities. They also help you find private apartments or shared housing options across the city through trusted partners.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<p><strong>Library</strong><br>Nebrija University offers a vast library network to support your academics. These facilities provide access to several resources, including books, journals, and more. You can use the OPAC Catalogue for resource discovery and manage your accounts online.</p><p><strong>Sports</strong><br>At Nebrija University, you can enjoy internal competitive sports, including basketball, futsal, volleyball, and paddle tennis. You can also go hiking, rock climbing, and many other activities.</p><p><strong>Laboratory</strong><br>You’ll have access to specialised laboratories at the university. These include a physics laboratory, computer lab, photography laboratory, language lab, and fine arts room.</p><p><strong>Cafeteria</strong><br>You can enjoy various meals and refreshments at the on-campus cafeterias Madrid-Princesa and La Berzosa.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
